ar with tenants","respected in court but disliked locally","considered unlucky","viewed as newly wealthy and socially insecure"],"noble-court-factions":["royal centralizers","old landed houses","merchant-aligned reformers","military traditionalists","temple coalition","regional autonomy bloc","heir-apparent's circle","quiet neutral caucus"],"noble-inheritance-pressures":["the recognized heir is unpopular","a younger branch has a stronger political alliance","documents supporting the succession are incomplete","the estate cannot be divided cleanly","an unrecognized claimant has appeared","the current holder refuses to name an heir"],"noble-marriage-pressures":["family expects a politically useful match","a prior promise conflicts with current strategy","the preferred match carries heavy debt","court factions oppose the arrangement","the intended partner has another attachment","marriage would transfer control of disputed property"],"noble-scandal-exposure":["estate accounts contain irregular payments","a relative's private conduct is becoming public","a retainer is selling correspondence","an old duel or legal dispute may reopen","the house concealed a politically dangerous guest","a patron's fall threatens everyone associated with them"],"noble-estate-conditions":["productive and well managed","profitable but overworked","rich in land but short of coin","recovering from disaster","maintained through heavy borrowing","politically valuable but economically weak","prosperous under a resented steward","declining behind an impressive public facade"]}}